.\design\architecture\initial description\action_popup.md:12:- `Run` asks the Electron-side action runner to start the action.
.\design\architecture\initial description\actions.md:30:  - `card-prompt`, containing the additional prompt entered when the card action runs.
.\design\architecture\initial description\actions.md:33:- The Electron-side action runner loads the definition by `id`, resolves placeholders, executes the full chain, and publishes execution events. React displays definitions and execution state but does not run or orchestrate actions.
.\designeleases\0_2_0\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:30:Schedule is an outlined text button with a calendar icon. Send, Stop, and Finish are icon buttons with tooltips; Schedule and command Run have no tooltips. `cancelPopupAction` stops the complete action run, including later `next` actions. `finishPopupAction` completes only the current agent conversation, allowing later actions to continue.
.\designeleases\0_2_0\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:52:- Given confirmation is open, `Stop sequence` stops complete action run; `Continue sequence` finishes current conversation and allows remaining actions to continue.
.\designeleases\0_2_0\F_156_when_approval_request_is_shown_hide_phrases.md:17:`ActionPhraseButtonsOwner` shows the predefined-phrase drawer when the scoped action run, or its selected persisted conversation, has `waitingForInput` status. An `agentApproval` event adds an unresolved approval to `ActionRun.approvals` and sets that same run status to `waitingForInput`. Because phrase visibility does not inspect `approvals`, the phrase drawer opens while `ActionAgentApprovals` shows the approval request and its decision buttons.
.\design\architecture\initial description\writingsunning_actions.md:11:- Actions can only execute through Electron. The Electron-side action runner owns definition lookup, validation, placeholder resolution, chaining, process execution, cancellation, and execution status.
.\design\architecture\initial description\writingsunning_actions.md:20:- The Electron-side action runner loads the persisted definition by `id`. Action names and labels are not identifiers and may be changed safely.
.\design\architecture\initial description\writingsunning_actions.md:21:- The action runner rejects an unknown `id`, an invalid context, invalid run-specific input, or a definition that is no longer valid.
.\design\architecture\initial description\writingsunning_actions.md:49:- When `needsWorkTree` is not set, the action runs in the currently opened project folder.
.\design\architecture\initial description\writingsunning_actions.md:67:- State-triggered actions use the same Electron-side action runner, card execution state, logs, errors, and cancellation behavior as manually started actions.
.\design\architecture\initial description\writingsunning_actions.md:97:- Every linked action is resolved by `id` and runs through the same Electron-side action runner.
.\design eature_descriptions\J_29_investigate_and_improve_stats_load_speed.md:107:- Duplicate conversations and action runs retain the existing canonical identity and deduplication behavior.
